# Prefixes this node must never blind-scan. One IPv4 CIDR per line;
# `#` starts a comment. Pass with --scan-exclude FILE.
#
# The reserved ranges (RFC 1918, loopback, link-local, CGNAT, multicast,
# documentation, benchmarking, 0/8, 240/4) and the US DoD /8s built into
# transpeer/scanner.py are always skipped and need not be listed. Add here:
#
#   - prefixes whose operators have asked not to be probed
#   - your own provider's ranges, if its acceptable-use policy forbids
#     scanning even at low rates
#   - other ranges you know to be sensitively monitored (government,
#     military, critical infrastructure). Published research-scanner
#     blocklists are a good start.
#
# An explicit --scan-range is not filtered by this file.

# 192.0.2.0/24        # example: an operator who asked to be left alone
# 198.51.100.0/24     # example
